## 7 Fusion

PSK-Realize groups the element-wise operations that can share one loop nest: an intermediate inside a group never reaches memory. `iN` is a group's input N, `sN` its step N.

In the functions `loss` reaches, 3 groups, 3 `let`s fused away:

```text
fn RMSNorm.apply — 8 lets, 2 groups, 2 launches saved
  %15 = add(i0,i1);sqrt(s0) [2 inputs, 2 steps]
  %18 = div(i0,i1);mul(s0,i2) [3 inputs, 2 steps]
fn loss — 6 lets, 1 groups, 1 launches saved
  %12 = sub(i0,i1);pow 2(s0) [2 inputs, 2 steps]
```

Over one call, fusion takes 39 launches to 30.

**Where each group ends**, and why each element-wise value outside a group is alone: what reads it. A value joins its reader's group when every reader is in that group, is element-wise and of the same shape, and the group's expression stays under its size limit.

| Value | Line |  | Reaches memory because |
|--------------------------|------------------------------------|-----------------|------------------------|
| `Linear.apply/%9` | `%9 : ℝ[..., Out] = add %7, b` | alone | the function's result |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%11` | `%11 : ℝ[..., model: D] = pow 2 x` | alone | read by `ms : ℝ[...] = mean axis model %11`: a reduction |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%15` | `%15 : ℝ[...] = sqrt %14` | ends a group of 2 | read by `%16 : ℝ[..., model: D] = div x, %15`, of another shape: a group is one loop nest over one shape |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%18` | `%18 : ℝ[..., model: D] = mul %16, γ` | ends a group of 2 | the function's result |
| `Block.apply/%13` | `%13 : ℝ[..., model: 4] = gelu %12` | alone | read by `%14 : ℝ[..., 4] = call Linear.apply{In = 4, Out = 4}(proj, %13)`: a call |
| `Block.apply/%15` | `%15 : ℝ[..., model: 4] = add x, %14` | alone | the function's result |
| `loss/%12` | `%12 : ℝ[batch: B, model: 4] = pow 2 %11` | ends a group of 2 | read by `%13 : ℝ[] = mean %12`: a reduction |

*Command:* `presk dump ../../tutorial/07_train.psk --stage realize --realize f32`

## 8 The machine and the layout plan

Each nest has a space of layouts (vector lanes, a split over workers, for a contraction a register tile, a k-block, a loop order, packing). The plan takes the point the profile's cost model predicts fastest; "within 1 + u" counts the points the model cannot tell from the best.

No profile: the cost model has no constants, so nothing is planned; every nest runs its default layout, the backend's natural vector width and no split.

## 9 The kernels and the host

PSK-Kernel is the loop nests the backends run: one kernel per distinct nest, under its type and its layout. The host program launches them, converting a value where a kernel reads it in another type.

```text
-- 10 kernels, 30 launches, f32
-- fusion: 39 launches without it, 9 saved (23%)
```

Each kernel under the sites that launch it, as the host recorded them:

```text
// k0: 4 launches at RMSNorm.apply/%11
kernel pow 2 (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %1[i0, i1] = (%0[i0, i1] * %0[i0, i1])
    }
  }
}
// k1: 4 launches at RMSNorm.apply/%12 (ms)
kernel mean axis model (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[batch: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    s0 = 0
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      s0 = (s0 + %0[i0, i1])
    }
    %1[i0] = (s0 / 4)
  }
}
// k2: 4 launches at RMSNorm.apply/%15 (fused)
kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 4], %1 : f32[]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    %2[i0] = sqrt((%0[i0] + %1[]))
  }
}
// k3: 4 launches at RMSNorm.apply/%18 (fused)
kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4], %1 : f32[batch: 4], %2 : f32[4]) -> %3 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %3[i0, i1] = ((%0[i0, i1] / %1[i0]) * %2[i1])
    }
  }
}
// k4: 3 launches at Block.apply/%13
kernel gelu (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %1[i0, i1] = (%0[i0, i1] * ((1 + erf((%0[i0, i1] / 1.4142135623730951))) / 2))
    }
  }
}
// k5: 3 launches at Linear.apply/%7
kernel dot (%0 : f32[batch: 4, 4], %1 : f32[4, 4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i2 in 0..4 {
      %2[i0, i2] = 0
    }
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      s0 = %0[i0, i1]
      for i2 in 0..4 {
        %2[i0, i2] = (%2[i0, i2] + (s0 * %1[i1, i2]))
      }
    }
  }
}
// k6: 3 launches at Linear.apply/%9
kernel add (%0 : f32[batch: 4, 4], %1 : f32[4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %2[i0, i1] = (%0[i0, i1] + %1[i1])
    }
  }
}
// k7: 3 launches at Block.apply/%15
kernel add (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4], %1 : f32[batch: 4, 4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %2[i0, i1] = (%0[i0, i1] + %1[i0, i1])
    }
  }
}
// k8: 1 launch at loss/%12 (fused)
kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4], %1 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4] {
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      %2[i0, i1] = ((%0[i0, i1] - %1[i0, i1]) * (%0[i0, i1] - %1[i0, i1]))
    }
  }
}
// k9: 1 launch at loss/%13
kernel mean (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[] {
  s0 = 0
  for i0 in 0..4 {
    for i1 in 0..4 {
      s0 = (s0 + %0[i0, i1])
    }
  }
  %1[] = (s0 / 16)
}
```

**The host**, as the C export prints it (§10): a function per Presk function, a fold a loop, each launch under the site it computes and each conversion where a kernel reads a value in another type.

```c
/* RMSNorm.apply at D = 4: 4 calls of the recording. */
static void presk_RMSNorm_apply(presk_arena *arena, const float *theta_gamma, const float *x, float *out)
{
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* RMSNorm.apply/%11 */
    float *t11 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    k0(x, t11, 0, 4);
    /* RMSNorm.apply/%12 (ms) */
    float *ms = presk_alloc(arena, 4 * sizeof(float));
    k1(t11, ms, 0, 4);
    /* RMSNorm.apply/%13 */
    float *t13 = presk_alloc(arena, 1 * sizeof(float));
    presk_fill(t13, PRESK_F32, 1e-6, 1);
    /* RMSNorm.apply/%15 (fused) */
    float *t15 = presk_alloc(arena, 4 * sizeof(float));
    k2(ms, t13, t15, 0, 4);
    /* RMSNorm.apply/%18 (fused) */
    k3(x, t15, theta_gamma, out, 0, 4);
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}

/* Linear.apply at In = 4, Out = 4: 3 calls of the recording. */
static void presk_Linear_apply(presk_arena *arena, const float *theta_w, const float *theta_b, const float *x, float *out)
{
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* Linear.apply/%7 */
    float *t7 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    k5(x, theta_w, t7, 0, 4);
    /* Linear.apply/%9 */
    k6(t7, theta_b, out, 0, 4);
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}

/* Block.apply: 3 calls of the recording. */
static void presk_Block_apply(presk_arena *arena, const float *theta_norm_gamma, const float *theta_proj_w, const float *theta_proj_b, const float *x, float *out)
{
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* Block.apply/%12 */
    float *t12 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    presk_RMSNorm_apply(arena, theta_norm_gamma, x, t12);
    /* Block.apply/%13 */
    float *t13 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    k4(t12, t13, 0, 4);
    /* Block.apply/%14 */
    float *t14 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    presk_Linear_apply(arena, theta_proj_w, theta_proj_b, t13, t14);
    /* Block.apply/%15 */
    k7(x, t14, out, 0, 4);
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}

/* Tower.apply: 1 call of the recording. */
static void presk_Tower_apply(presk_arena *arena, const float *theta_blocks_norm_gamma, const float *theta_blocks_proj_w, const float *theta_blocks_proj_b, const float *theta_final_gamma, const float *x, float *out)
{
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* Tower.apply/%9 */
    /* a fold of 3 iterations: one loop over its 3 iterations */
    const float *x_2 = x;
    float *x_buf[2] = {presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float)), presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float))};
    for (int64_t l = 0; l < 3; l++) {
        presk_Block_apply(arena, theta_blocks_norm_gamma + l * 4, theta_blocks_proj_w + l * 16, theta_blocks_proj_b + l * 4, x_2, x_buf[l % 2]);
        x_2 = x_buf[l % 2];
    }
    /* Tower.apply/%11 */
    presk_RMSNorm_apply(arena, theta_final_gamma, x_2, out);
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}

void presk_loss(presk_arena *arena, const presk_loss_in *in, presk_loss_out *out)
{
    const float *theta_blocks_norm_gamma = in->theta_blocks_norm_gamma;
    const float *theta_blocks_proj_w = in->theta_blocks_proj_w;
    const float *theta_blocks_proj_b = in->theta_blocks_proj_b;
    const float *theta_final_gamma = in->theta_final_gamma;
    const float *batch_0 = in->batch_0;
    const float *batch_1 = in->batch_1;
    float *result = presk_alloc(arena, 1 * sizeof(float));
    const size_t mark = presk_mark(arena);
    /* loss/%9 */
    float *t9 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    presk_Tower_apply(arena, theta_blocks_norm_gamma, theta_blocks_proj_w, theta_blocks_proj_b, theta_final_gamma, batch_0, t9);
    /* loss/%12 (fused) */
    float *t12 = presk_alloc(arena, 16 * sizeof(float));
    k8(t9, batch_1, t12, 0, 4);
    /* loss/%13 */
    k9(t12, result, 0, 0);
    out->result = result;
    presk_release(arena, mark);
}
```

*Command:* `presk dump ../../tutorial/07_train.psk --stage kernel --entry loss --dim B=4 --realize f32`

## 10 Targets

**Native.** The Cranelift backend compiles each of the 10 kernels to machine code at its first launch, in process, and the host program of §9 runs them.

**C.** `presk export --target c` writes the entry as a C program that computes the native backend's bits (statement C1):

```text
presk export: `loss` at B = 4 in f32: 30 launches (0 dead, on one thread) of 10 kernels, 4 functions besides the entry's and 1 loop, an arena of 1088 bytes (2688 released nothing), into $DOC/artifacts/c; `make -C $DOC/artifacts/c check` builds it and compares it with the native backend
```

| File | Lines |
|-------------------|----------|
| `Makefile` | 22 |
| `README.md` | 66 |
| `kernels.c` | 201 |
| `main.c` | 113 |
| `model.c` | 109 |
| `model.h` | 35 |
| `presk_libm.c` | 2680 |
| `presk_rt.c` | 743 |
| `presk_rt.h` | 347 |

The first contraction, `k5`, as C:

```c
// kernel dot (%0 : f32[batch: 4, 4], %1 : f32[4, 4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, 4] {
//   for i0 in 0..4 {
//     for i2 in 0..4 {
//       %2[i0, i2] = 0
//     }
//     for i1 in 0..4 {
//       s0 = %0[i0, i1]
//       for i2 in 0..4 {
//         %2[i0, i2] = (%2[i0, i2] + (s0 * %1[i1, i2]))
//       }
//     }
//   }
// }
// lo, hi: the range of i0 in 0..4, the outermost loop, which a thread split divides
static void k5(const float *restrict in0, const float *restrict in1, float *restrict out, int64_t lo, int64_t hi) {
    int64_t i0 = 0, i1 = 0, i2 = 0;
    float s0 = 0.0f;
    for (i0 = lo; i0 < hi; i0++) {
        for (i2 = 0; i2 < 4; i2++) {
            out[i0 * 4 + i2] = 0.0f;
        }
        for (i1 = 0; i1 < 4; i1++) {
            s0 = in0[i0 * 4 + i1];
            for (i2 = 0; i2 < 4; i2++) {
                out[i0 * 4 + i2] = out[i0 * 4 + i2] + s0 * in1[i1 * 4 + i2];
            }
        }
    }
}
```

`make -C $DOC/artifacts/c check` builds it and compares its outputs with the native backend's, bit for bit.

*Command:* `presk export ../../tutorial/07_train.psk --target c --entry loss --dim B=4 --realize f32 --threads 10 -o $DOC/artifacts/c`

## 11 Measured

What one run measured on this machine: the realization natively against the exact reference, a call timed, each kernel's time beside the model's prediction, and the host's time by phase. The one section that changes from run to run.

Not measured: `--measure` was not given. Every other section is deterministic; this one would hold times.

## 12 Sites through every stage

A site is named `<function>/%<n>` at every stage, which is what lets one value be followed from PSK-Core to the C.

By default, the three largest shares of the solver's estimate (the three largest bounds without a solve), then the three nests of the most predicted time a call; `--site` names others.

**`loss/%6`**

| Stage |  |
|------------------|------------------------------------|
| PSK-Core (§3) | `%6 : ℝ[batch: B, model: 4] = pow 2 %5` in `loss` |
| Envelope (§6.1) | \|v\| ≤ 7.476e0, 16 elements |
| Sensitivity (§6.2) | 1.000e0 |
| Type (§6.3) | `f32`, decision |
| Optimizer (§5) | `%12 : ℝ[batch: B, model: 4] = pow 2 %11` in `loss`: `loss/%6` under a new number, no rule changed it |
| Fusion (§7) | ends a group of 2: read by `%13 : ℝ[] = mean %12`: a reduction |
| Kernel (§9) | `k8`: `kernel fused 2 steps (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4], %1 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %2 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]` |
| C (§10) | `k8` in `kernels.c`, launched by `presk_loss` in `model.c`, the launch commented `loss/%12` |

**`RMSNorm.apply/%3`**

| Stage |  |
|------------------|------------------------------------|
| PSK-Core (§3) | `%3 : ℝ[..., model: D] = pow 2 x` in `RMSNorm.apply` |
| Envelope (§6.1) | \|v\| ≤ 4.021e0, 16 elements |
| Sensitivity (§6.2) | 1.147e0 |
| Type (§6.3) | `f32`, decision |
| Optimizer (§5) | `%11 : ℝ[..., model: D] = pow 2 x` in `RMSNorm.apply`: `RMSNorm.apply/%3` under a new number, no rule changed it |
| Fusion (§7) | alone: read by `ms : ℝ[...] = mean axis model %11`: a reduction |
| Kernel (§9) | `k0`: `kernel pow 2 (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]` |
| C (§10) | `k0` in `kernels.c`, launched by `presk_RMSNorm_apply` in `model.c`, the launch commented `RMSNorm.apply/%11` |

**`loss/%7`**

| Stage |  |
|------------------|------------------------------------|
| PSK-Core (§3) | `%7 : ℝ[] = mean %6` in `loss` |
| Envelope (§6.1) | \|v\| ≤ 2.104e0, 1 element, condition number 1.000e0 |
| Sensitivity (§6.2) | 1.000e0 |
| Type (§6.3) | `f32`, decision |
| Optimizer (§5) | `%13 : ℝ[] = mean %12` in `loss`: `loss/%7` under a new number, no rule changed it |
| Fusion (§7) | not an element-wise operation |
| Kernel (§9) | `k9`: `kernel mean (%0 : f32[batch: 4, model: 4]) -> %1 : f32[]` |
| C (§10) | `k9` in `kernels.c`, launched by `presk_loss` in `model.c`, the launch commented `loss/%13` |

